  "lore": "The Chimera is a tripartite blasphemy, a living testament to the world\u2019s capacity for discord. These horrors haunt the jagged crags and desolate ruins of the high reaches, where their multiple eyes can survey the valleys below. To witness a Chimera is to see nature unraveled: the prideful lion, the resilient goat, and the venomous serpent fused into a singular, predatory engine.\n\nIts hunting method is a chaotic symphony of violence. While the lion\u2019s head rends armor with primal ferocity, the goat\u2019s horns batter the dazed, and the serpent-tail strikes with necrotizing precision. Most devastating, however, is the gout of alchemical fire erupted from its throat, capable of turning mountain paths into molten glass.\n\nIn local folklore, the Chimera is rarely viewed as a mere beast of burden or evolution. Instead, it is whispered to be a \"Curse of the Broken Veil\"\u2014a manifestation of ancient alchemical folly or divine displeasure. To hear its discordant roar, a terrifying blend of feline bellow and shrill bleat, is considered a death omen. It does not merely hunt for sustenance; it exists as a sentinel of ruin, guarding secrets that were never meant for mortal eyes.",
